---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import { getSitePage, REVIEWED_DATE, REVIEWED_ISO } from "../data/sitePages";

const page = getSitePage("/cookies/");
---

<BaseLayout
  title={page.title}
  description={page.description}
  alternateMd="/cookies/index.md"
  pageType="WebPage"
  dateModified={REVIEWED_ISO}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Cookies" }]} />
  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <h1>Cookies and local storage</h1>
      <p class="small">Last reviewed: {REVIEWED_DATE}</p>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--ink-2)">
        This site is static and has no account, cart, language preference or saved quotation. It therefore sets no
        functional or advertising storage of its own. The only cookies that may appear are security cookies from the
        hosting and content-delivery layer.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What this page covers</h2>
      <p>
        This page lists the cookies that may be set when you request a page, explains why a consent banner is not
        shown, and tells you how to block or delete cookies. It covers this website only. Email, WhatsApp, a carrier's
        tracking page and any other site you reach by a link have their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Cookies that may be set</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Cookie name</th><th scope="col">Set by</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Duration</th><th scope="col">Type</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>__cf_bm</code></td><td>Cloudflare</td><td>Bot management: distinguishes a browser from automated traffic and helps block abuse</td><td>30 minutes</td><td>Strictly necessary</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>cf_clearance</code></td><td>Cloudflare</td><td>May be set by the CDN when a security challenge is required, so a cleared browser can continue</td><td>Session</td><td>Strictly necessary</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        Cloudflare may not set both cookies on every request. A challenge and its clearance cookie appear only when
        the network decides that a request needs one. The cookies carry no advertising identifier and are not used
        to build a profile of your interests.
      </p>

      <h2>3. What we do not use</h2>
      <p>
        There are no analytics cookies, advertising cookies, retargeting pixels, social-media embeds, video players,
        heatmaps, session replays or A/B testing tools on this site. There is no Google Analytics tag, no advertising
        conversion tag and no newsletter script. We do not embed a third-party map, review widget or customer-chat
        service that would load a tracker.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Local and session storage</h2>
      <p>
        Our site code does not write to <code>localStorage</code> or <code>sessionStorage</code>. The site has no
        saved quote, dark-mode switch, currency selector or account state to remember. We checked the site source at
        this review; a future change that introduces browser storage will be added to this page before it is
        released. A browser or extension you installed may store its own data, but that is outside this site's code.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Why there is no consent banner</h2>
      <p>
        Consent is not required for a cookie that is strictly necessary to provide a service you requested, such as
        a security cookie used to deliver the page and protect it from abuse. We use only that category. If we add
        analytics, advertising or any non-essential tool, this page will name it and a consent mechanism will be
        added before the tool goes live. The site will not load a non-essential tracker first and ask later.
      </p>

      <h2>6. How to block or delete cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Every current browser lets you view, block and delete cookies in its privacy or site-data settings. Because
        the only cookies here are security-related, blocking them may cause a challenge loop or stop a protected
        request from loading; the content itself has no login or cart to break. Deleting cookies after a visit
        removes the browser copy. For a site-specific choice, use the browser's exception list rather than blocking
        all cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        If you want to know what a specific request stored, email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Cookies`}>{site.email}</a> with the subject “Cookies” and the page
        URL. Our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> covers the data we hold when you send an enquiry or place an
        order.
      </p>
      <p class="small">
        Related policies: <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> · <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> ·
        <a href="/refund-policy/">Returns</a> · <a href="/shipping-delivery/">Shipping</a> ·
        <a href="/declarations/">Declarations</a> · <a href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial standards</a> ·
        <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> · <a href="/corrections/">Corrections</a> ·
        <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> · <a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility</a> ·
        <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
